; @vlcn.io/crsqlite runs its own "install" lifecycle script (nodejs-install-helper.js)
; before this package's own postinstall ever fires. That script still uses the
; Node <22 "assert { type: "json" }" import-attribute syntax, which is a hard
; syntax error on Node 24 -- so it crashes before patch-crsqlite.sh gets a chance
; to run. Disabling automatic scripts and driving install order explicitly via
; `npm run native:setup` (patch crsqlite -> build better-sqlite3's N-API addon ->
; fetch crsqlite's prebuilt extension -> download Puppeteer's Chrome build) is the
; only way to make a plain `npm ci`/`npm install` succeed on Node 24.
ignore-scripts=true
